Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Exit Resampling for Subsurface Scattering", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ecfccafd-4baa-48f1-a332-c183d899e72a"],

Cell["The missing escape-probability weight ...", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9966641863219957`*^9, 
  3.9966641926185303`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ca1aa6d3-fe5c-4327-82f6-\
09102bcf50f1"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook picks back up a derivation that stalled years ago. The first \
section below is the original work: the corrected exit-resampling \
distribution for the classical half-space case, matching Eq. 74 of d'Eon & \
Krivanek, 'Zero-Variance Theory for Efficient Subsurface Scattering', Sec. \
6.6.2. That part was reviewed (together with Eugene d\[CloseCurlyQuote]Eon) \
and found meaningful at the time. What was missing was the weight correction \
needed to actually use the resampled direction without introducing bias -- \
that's the new section at the end.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9966626018722734`*^9, 3.9966626027206464`*^9}, {
  3.996662637732422*^9, 
  3.9966626497893867`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6362a2b2-a117-4488-a2cc-\
da07dfc1603d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Attempt 1 -- original derivation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"36333977-bb3f-4f31-989b-4812a318b242"],

Cell["\<\
Note: this first attempt's setup line uses ExpIntegralEi[x], but the comment \
right below it describes E1(x) -- these are genuinely different functions (Ei \
grows, E1 decays). It looks like a typo when first typing the formula. It did \
not propagate, though: the closed-form ePDF/eCDF derived a few lines down \
correctly use Gamma[0,x], which is exactly E1(x) by a standard identity \
(Gamma[0,x] == ExpIntegralE[1,x]), confirmed numerically before trusting any \
of this further. Kept here exactly as originally worked out, typo included, \
for an honest record.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11ccda26-7487-46e5-879b-6b613c5e0e03"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
exitProbDist = E^(x + x/u)/(
  1 - E^x x ExpIntegralEi[
     x]);         

(* Subscript[E, 1] is the 'first exp integral' : the integral from 1 to \
Infinity of Exp[-x t]/t dt, like in the Milne equation *)
(* for the above, see d'Eon/Krivanek -> Zero-Variance Theory for Efficient \
Subsurface Scattering *)
(* mu domain is -1 to 0 as we're trying to reach the boundary so directions \
go upward *)
(* x > 0 as we're in medium seeking to escape *)
\[ScriptCapitalD] = 
 Simplify[ProbabilityDistribution[exitProbDist, {u, -1, 0}, 
   Assumptions -> x > 0, Method -> \"Normalize\"]]
\[ScriptCapitalD] /. 
 ProbabilityDistribution -> 
  Integrate (* let's check it integrates to 1 *)
CDF[\[ScriptCapitalD]] (* from PDF find the CDF *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9966594971518946`*^9, 3.9966594993742185`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[220]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dceaaaf8-c68e-4fa3-94e3-60922c57de0e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ProbabilityDistribution", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{"x", "+", 
      FractionBox["x", "\[FormalX]"]}]], 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", "x"], " ", "x", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Gamma", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "x"}], "]"}]}]}]], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[FormalX]", ",", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"x", ">", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9963399167233934`*^9, 3.996659366919225*^9, 
  3.996661332566893*^9, 3.996662774368439*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[226]=",ExpressionUUID->"d6fa94ae-0c0d-4434-ac0a-94cf9d1578da"],

Cell[BoxData["1"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9963399167233934`*^9, 3.996659366919225*^9, 
  3.996661332566893*^9, 3.996662775049017*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[227]=",ExpressionUUID->"3d12963a-2ab7-4bca-9ec2-afe69a530399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
  RowBox[{"\[FormalX]", ",", 
   TagBox[GridBox[{
      {"\[Piecewise]", GridBox[{
         {"1", 
          RowBox[{"\[FormalX]", "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}]},
         {
          FractionBox[
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "-", 
            RowBox[{"\[FormalX]", " ", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
              RowBox[{"x", "+", 
               FractionBox["x", "\[FormalX]"]}]]}], "+", 
            RowBox[{
