Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
A faster E1 approximation (single smooth formula, no piecewise switch)\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e24a2d8f-dc25-4fce-85a1-443cbd8e5bbc"],

Cell["\<\
Kept for reference -- checked numerically against Abramowitz & Stegun's \
piecewise rational approximation (what the C++ implementation actually uses): \
this single-formula version is measurably less accurate across most of the \
tested range (roughly 1e-3 to 1e-4 relative error here, vs 1e-6 to 1e-8 for \
the piecewise A&S form) but has no seam at x=1 and stays smooth everywhere. \
Worth knowing which property mattered more when this was reached for -- raw \
accuracy, or smoothness for some other symbolic use.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4af04d2-86e2-486a-aa4a-100df71657e5"],

Cell["\<\
E1[u_] := Module[{y, G, b, w, E},
  y = 0.5772156649015328606;
  G = Exp[-y];
  b = Sqrt[(2 (1 - G))/(G (2 - G))];
  w = ((1 - G) (G^2 - 6 G + 12))/(3 G (2 - G)^2 b);
  q = 20/47 u Sqrt[31/26];
  h = 1/(1 + u Sqrt[u]) + (w*q)/(1 + q);
  E = (Exp[-u] Log[1 + G/u - (1 - G)/(h + b*u)^2])/(
   G + (1 - G) Exp[-u/(1 - G)])
  ]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[258]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1e4a5784-d8bd-441a-b5e5-3e252ebc01be"],

